' PresentationString.puml
@startuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

'Bring in the shared types
!include ./InternationalString.puml
!include ./TechString.puml


class PresentationString{
  +techValue: TechString
  +presentationValue: InternationalString
}

note right of PresentationString
SCHEMAHINTS v0.1
title: PresentationString
additionalProperties: false
required: [techValue, presentationValue]

field techValue:
  $ref: /core/commonLib/TechString
  ' Presentation string 

field presentationValue:
  $ref: /core/commonLib/InternationalString
  ' string (for enums will be translated) that will be
  ' presented to a human traveler or service agent

end note

note top of PresentationString
PresentationString is where a schema property is defined
by an enum, which needs to be mapped (via a translation table lookup 
to provide the string to present to a human observer got the selected)

techValue - is the enum value (for use by applications)
presentationValue is the InternationalString value in the lang/locale/encoding
as selected for the component using the PresentationString schema
end note

@enduml

